            "source": "https://doi.org/10.6028/NIST.SP.800-66r2",
            "description": "HIPAA Security Rule safeguards implemented by this system. NIST SP 800-66 Rev. 2 (Implementing the HIPAA Security Rule) is the catalog source; each requirement carries its 45 CFR 164 citation in the hipaa-citation prop. Not claimed: GAP-05 (Lambda outside the VPC), GAP-06 (concurrency, DLQ, tracing), and GAP-08 (API access logging and throttling) remain open; patient data lifecycle (deletion, export, retention) and API-layer authentication are known gaps outside GAPS.md; and Physical Safeguards (164.310) are inherited from AWS.",
            "implemented-requirements": [
              {
                "uuid": "6802a85e-5eb8-4b76-9e55-8ac4643d48f2",
                "control-id": "hipaa-164.312-a-2-iv",
                "description": "PHI at rest is encrypted under a customer-managed KMS key with automatic rotation. The uploads bucket uses SSE-KMS with S3 Bucket Keys (GAP-01) and the submissions table uses server-side encryption with the same key (GAP-02). The Rego policies block any S3 bucket that holds PHI without SSE-KMS under an aws_kms_key, and any DynamoDB table without a customer-managed key. CloudTrail log buckets are a documented exception (account activity, not PHI).",
                "props": [
