                "uuid": "90587faa-4fce-4e08-8e5b-f36351c9ae5d",
                "control-id": "hipaa-164.312-a-1",
                "description": "The intake Lambda role is reduced from dynamodb:* and s3:* to dynamodb:PutItem on the submissions table, s3:PutObject on the uploads/ prefix, and the KMS actions needed for its key (GAP-07). Pipeline access is split: pull requests assume a read-only plan role that cannot decrypt PHI, and only pushes to main assume the apply role. The Rego policy fails the gate on any wildcard action in an IAM Allow statement; red PR run 38051205888 shows the gate blocking a reintroduced dynamodb:*. Continuously, an EventBridge rule alerts on any role-policy or trust-policy change made outside the pipeline's apply role; AWS Config managed rules do not evaluate inline role policies, so this alert is the live-state control for this requirement.",
